    "checks": [
      "Only an existing carriage house or garage may become an ADU. It may be enlarged, but then the district dimensional rules apply (1.04.005(c)(4))",
      "Efficiency or one-bedroom unit only. At most two occupants (1.04.005(c)(6) and (7))",
      "The principal house must be an owner-occupied single-family dwelling. The ADU must be removed or converted back when that ends (1.04.005(c)(1) and (2))",
      "The ADU must be licensed under the city rental housing rules and tenants registered (1.04.005(c)(9)). Article 1761 lists an ADU as a tenant-occupied unit",
      "Design must be consistent with the principal building. A unit added above a garage may not be larger than the garage footprint or hang over it (1.04.005(c)(10) and (11))",
      "If the required off-street parking cannot be provided on site, the ADU may not be approved (1.04.005(c)(5))",
      "An accessory building may not exceed 50% of the first floor building area of the principal structure (1304.02 7.01(b)(2))",
      "1303.06(g)(2) also says a rear building that meets all use, height and area rules may be used as an ADU if the principal unit is owner-occupied. How this relates to 1.04.005 is not clear. Ask the Zoning Officer"
